equests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"0139bf98a3d97fbedc52e94b862e197e964ad2d34c425a25bd22b61339b3ca87"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"single:E3,F4,G5,T12,T5e,project.portability","usage":{"input_tokens":9544,"output_tokens":1511,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"0f9298f6f4c25a626eaae3e6f52edd714674b87889dd0b1b1a8e51fbc9337c56"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"single:COH,E1,E2,F1,T2,T4","usage":{"input_tokens":7938,"output_tokens":2047,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"3ec6cf5c12d48e61c3dc78f94cbf3ce4b4a87772fc9f2f9bde4e96c850751ddd"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":23365,"output_tokens":1330,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"2314b4d44cebd9f75a583a04c51c894b11207dc25b44cf4d219c68452c115a99"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":54821,"output_tokens":1480,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"fae68b1ffe20431afc0ef9be7f23f33f2f467917c2e150a7922dfc3e32eb125b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":24579,"output_tokens":1119,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"de806f988152792c112477f9d2f000c03f6e8f11201d177382ede3ec49cdea2a"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":80779,"output_tokens":1531,"requests":5}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"7dd530ca936193d2cd93be4546c916a7a0622d825ab846ac73e11888d1185d6b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":275166,"output_tokens":4656,"requests":10}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define \"endpoint family\" and the outcome-to-scope attribution rule so the endpoint/provider fuse thresholds are deterministically computable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","F1","T2","T4"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"provider scope additionally spans two endpoint families\"","\"counting only the eligible exhausted-transient (`exhausted_transient`) outcomes attributed to that scope\"","No definition of \"endpoint family\" or the attribution rule appears anywhere in the plan."],"finding":"The plan repeatedly relies on \"endpoint family\" and outcome-to-scope \"attribution\" as load-bearing concepts for the fuse (provider scope requires spanning ≥2 endpoint families; counters count outcomes \"attributed to that scope\"), but never defines what constitutes an endpoint family or the rule by which an outcome is attributed to an endpoint vs provider scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4e5901dd28af3952","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 / Fuse counter semantics section / AC line 3","norm_id":"na9074c1264234128","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer must decide whether two Jira REST calls belong to the same or different endpoint families to evaluate the provider fuse threshold.","Determining which scope a given failed outcome increments."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a short definition (e.g., endpoint family = the Jira API resource group such as issues, transitions, labels; provider = the tenant/host) and state how each outcome maps to exactly one endpoint-family scope and one provider scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define 'endpoint family' and the deterministic rule that attributes each OperationOutcome to an endpoint/provider fuse scope (e.g. derived from FailureScope + a stable endpoint/family key), so the >=2-family provider threshold and per-scope counters are implementable and testable.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 3: 'provider scope additionally spans two endpoint families'","Fuse semantics: 'Each fuse scope (endpoint family; provider = >=2 endpoint families) owns its own consecutive counter ... counting only the eligible exhausted-transient outcomes attributed to that scope'","search of src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler for 'endpoint family' returned (no matches)","operation_outcome.FailureScope defines endpoint/provider/tenant but no family grouping key"],"finding":"The fuse mechanism depends on classifying and attributing outcomes to 'endpoint families' (provider scope requires the failing outcomes to span >=2 endpoint families, and per-scope counters are 'attributed to that scope'), but the plan never defines what an endpoint family is or how a given OperationOutcome is mapped to one. The existing FailureScope enum (none/ticket/endpoint/tenant/provider/global) has no family grouping, and the term appears nowhere in the codebase.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5f6bcc81a03cc28d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 3 + Fuse counter semantics ('provider = >=2 endpoint families'; 'attributed to that scope')","norm_id":"n616a084455cd63ea","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two exhausted_transient outcomes hit different Jira DC endpoints — implementer cannot deterministically decide whether they belong to the same family (no reset) or different families (provider-scope tripping)","Attributing an outcome to a scope's per-scope counter requires a family key that is undefined"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a definition tying each outcome to a scope key: e.g. an endpoint family = the (provider, endpoint-class) pair derived from the adapter/route that produced the outcome, with the mapping specified so the coordinator can bucket exhausted_transient outcomes per family and count distinct families for provider scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify whether/how retry_not_before deferrals durably suppress re-attempting a persistently-failing endpoint across passes (or state explicitly that per-pass re-tripping plus retry_not_before honoring is the intended cross-pass backoff), so the volatile fuse and durable deferral do not conflict.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Fuse semantics: 'the coordinator carries no durable state between passes ... re-trips the fuse in each subsequent pass'","AC5: 'Remaining matching work is explicitly deferred with reason/scope/retry_not_before'","ADR 0103 line 104: S3 'owns the fuse and durable-deferral consumer that reads the retry_not_before/disposition tags'"],"finding":"The plan deliberately makes the fuse counter per-pass and non-durable ('An endpoint that keeps failing simply re-trips the fuse in each subsequent pass'), but does not specify how this interacts with the durable, cross-pass retry_not_before deferral that AC5 promises and that ADR 0103 assigns to S3 ('durable-deferral consumer that reads the retry_not_before/disposition tags'). As written, a permanently-degraded endpoint is re-attempted up to the threshold every pass with no cross-pass backoff, which may contradict the intent of retry_not_before.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb2b5a7575481058","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fuse counter semantics ('Per-pass and in-memory, never durable across passes') vs AC line 5 (retry_not_before)","norm_id":"n1e4160a8c491a3f2","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An endpoint is down for hours: every pass re-accumulates the threshold of exhausted_transient work before the fuse trips again, spending budget on known-dead work each pass","A deferred plan carries retry_not_before in the future but the next pass re-attempts it anyway because the fuse counter reset to zero"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verificati